+## 2026-10-23T12:43:26.6697187+08:00 (UTC+08:00) - Recover known reader-blocked SQLite commits
+
+- Reproduced the .2 permanent queue suspension with actual provider bytecode and bundled SQLite: an explicit reader snapshot blocks COMMIT, rollback succeeds, but unlock/retry cannot drain. The same native failure reproduces through the real Minecraft background worker and native block/container/drop producers. Prior .2 source, JAR, worlds and logs remain retained.
+- Build .3 permits retry only when the direct Xerial connection reports typed SQLITE_BUSY, current and next transaction modes are DEFERRED, rollback succeeds and queued writes are reconstructable. Xerial commit() runs COMMIT followed by BEGIN; an IMMEDIATE/EXCLUSIVE next BEGIN can fail after successful commit. DEFERRED acquires no lock. Other commit/driver/wrapper/mode, failed rollback and legacy-batch outcomes retain the uncertainty fence. No SQL error-message matching or guessed durable outcome.
+- Added a compile-only SQLite dependency to common and shared the existing 3.47.2.0 version across platform declarations. NeoForge nested selectable driver packaging remains intact; no root SQLite classes. Minecraft/bootstrap/runtime storage code is not substituted in native runs.
+- Java 21 :neoforge:build succeeds. Expanded actual-provider standalone suite passes 53 assertions, including original writer/prefix/batch/concurrent/uncertain cases, exact ordinary/batch reader retry parameters, three current/next mode controls and wrapped BUSY after successful real commit. A fresh NeoForge 21.1.248 reader fixture passes 22 native and 11 clean-restart checks. Broader writer/normal acceptance is recorded by the consuming Citizens repository when complete.
+- Pending work remains in memory. Unflushed termination, full-device failures, uncertain-outcome administration, retention/load, MySQL and wider integration/client acceptance remain open. No production or deferred client fixture changes. Author and committer use A-BenLi06 <ben_li06@outlook.com>.
